  <item>
    <title>Richmond: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/richmond-ca</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-richmond-ca</guid>
    <pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>45-day urgency interim ordinance (Gov. Code 65858). As amended, the city may accept and process applications but may not approve them or issue permits. No applications were pending. Staff said they would return before it lapses to seek an extension. Extended: the city&#x27;s CEQA Notice of Exemption for Urgency Ordinance No. 13-26 N.S. says the moratorium runs an additional 22 months and 15 days, through Sept 15, 2028; Richmond Confidential reports the council vote was unanimous</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Gilroy: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/gilroy-ca</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-gilroy-ca</guid>
    <pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Council unanimously adopted a 45-day urgency moratorium, effective immediately, barring the city from accepting, processing or approving applications and entitlements for new data centers while it drafts zoning and operating standards. Does not affect the approved Amazon facility under construction in northeast Gilroy. May be extended to a two-year maximum. Council unanimously extended it on Oct 19, 2026; it now expires Sept 3, 2027 and can be extended once more for 12 months</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Arcata: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/arcata-ca</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-arcata-ca</guid>
    <pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Urgency Ordinance No. 1594 (Gov Code 65858) bars the city from receiving, accepting, processing or approving data center land-use applications. Ordinance No. 1595, adopted 5-0 at a special meeting on Oct 28, 2026, extends it 10 months and 15 days, through September 15, 2027; one further one-year extension is permitted</description>
  </item>
